{"kind":"assert","text":"Thread record-detail carry: five of seven commits carried onto current main c086ee1e on request/thread-record-detail-v2, and the union decision in ui/src/lib/rows.ts is made. Recording it before I build on it, because it is the design choice Hugh authorised and the next reviewer should see it stated rather than inferred from a diff.\n\nCARRIED CLEANLY: 26e25bdf, 5ea95ce4, 39fc1720, bd81fbb1, and the rows.ts half of 75a1eb33. Planner's account of the conflicts held exactly. The internal/service/uidist collisions are the generated embed and I took the incoming side without reading it, to be regenerated with make ui at the end rather than hand-merged. The RequestList.tsx conflict in 39fc1720 was keep-both as described: main's vocabulary binding stays, the branch's lifting of sort, query and population into a view prop replaces the useState trio.\n\nTHE UNION, as resolved in rows.ts. RowState becomes the union of both sides rather than either: the four live words and stale from main, the branch's satisfied, cancelled, reneged and withdrawn, and main's awaiting ratification. The comment above it claimed four words and no fifth, which both sides had already outgrown, so it now says which words a live row may use and why the closed ones do not weaken that rule. Population gains a sixth member, ratifiable, labelled awaiting ratification.\n\nWHAT I DID NOT DO, and this is the part worth stating. I did not make ratification a sixth workRows population. ratificationRows takes the vocabulary and returns rows plus ratifiers; workRows takes a population and returns WorkRow[]. Pretending they are the same shape is how the awaiting-ratification state would quietly become a filter over commitments and stop counting what it exists to count. The caller dispatches on the tab instead. inPopulation gains an explicit ratifiable case returning false, with a comment that it is unreachable rather than empty, so the switch stays exhaustive over Population and a seventh population is a compile error rather than a silently empty tab.\n\nREMAINING: four conflict regions across 86 lines in ui/src/components/RequestList.tsx, plus ui/test/dom.test.mjs, all from 75a1eb33 against merged 511335e7. That is exactly where the summary links become tabs and where ratificationRows either survives or does not -- the region where planner nearly shipped the regression recorded in 4729a06a and 56c8f6d4. I stopped here rather than resolving it quickly, and will finish it, then carry 16c1f7ac and 43daa5f0 and close codex's two findings. Nothing is published and no review is requested yet."}